# Agent Workflow — ai-project-docs

Rules **exclusive to this repository** (`Context-Generator-for-AI-Agent`). Other projects have their own `.cursor/rules/` — do not reuse these.

This rule is **user-managed**. It complements `ai-project-docs.mdc` (PKM-generated in this repo).

## Language — English only

All project documentation must be written in **English**:

- Markdown: `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `docs/`, `.ai-docs/`, module `README.md` files
- Cursor rules: `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` (except YAML frontmatter `description` may stay short)
- Code comments that explain *why* (not identifiers or API names)
- Commit messages and PR descriptions when touching docs

Do not add or leave Portuguese (or other non-English) prose in documentation files. User chat may be in any language; written project artifacts are English.

## Before any change

1. **Classify the task** (pick one):
   - `architecture` — module boundaries or pipeline structure
   - `feature` — new step, analyzer, generator, detector, or CLI flag
   - `bugfix` — fix existing behavior
   - `test` — add or update tests
   - `docs` — Markdown, README, or generated context
   - `config` — RuntimeConfig, tsconfig, CLI flags
   - `dependency` — package.json / npm
   - `agent-export` — exporters, Cursor rules, agent packs

2. **Load minimum context** (in order):
   - Always: `AGENTS.md` (repo root — authoritative)
   - Then: `.ai-docs/agent-navigation.md` → section for your task type
   - Then: documents listed in that section (e.g. `docs/architecture.md`, `.ai-docs/implementation-guide.md`)
   - Before editing a module: `src/<module>/README.md`
   - For type decisions: `src/domain/README.md` + `src/knowledge/README.md`

3. **Only then** open relevant source files. Do not start blindly in `src/`.

## Work routing

| Work | Where to implement | Key files |
|---|---|---|
| New analyzer | `src/analyzers/` + plugin in `src/plugins/` | `PluginRegistry`, `pipeline-integration.ts` |
| New pipeline step | `src/domain/pipeline.ts` + module handler + `pipeline-orchestrator.ts` | `ANALYSIS_PIPELINE` |
| New Markdown renderer | `src/docs/markdown-renderers/` + `src/templates/markdown-template.ts` | Consumes `ProjectKnowledge` only |
| New agent exporter | `src/exporters/` + `exporter-registry.ts` | Consumes `ProjectKnowledge` only |
| New CLI flag / env | `src/config/index.ts` | Only place for `process.argv` / `process.env` |
| Tech detection | `src/detectors/` | No directory walk |
| Repo scan | `src/scanner/` | Respects `RepositoryBoundary` |
| Orchestration | `src/core/` | No domain logic, scan, AI, or doc I/O |
| Pure types | `src/domain/` | No Node imports, no behavior |

## Golden rule — PKM

- **Generators and exporters** receive `ProjectKnowledge` — never `RepositoryInfo`, `TechnologyProfile`, or `DocumentationPlan` directly.
- **Analyzers** enrich PKM via `PluginContributions`; do not mutate PKM or re-scan the repo.
- **Renderers** are presentation-only: no `fs`, no OpenRouter, no repo analysis.
- Source of truth: `.ai-docs/knowledge/project-knowledge.json`

## Checklist before finishing

```bash
npm run build   # zero TypeScript strict errors
npm test        # tests passing
```

If architecture or PKM sections changed: update `docs/architecture.md` and/or affected READMEs (in English).

If project context changed: regenerate with `node dist/cli.js . --export-agents --target cursor`.

## Hard stops

- Put scan, detect, AI, or doc-write logic in `src/cli.ts` or `src/core/` (outside orchestration)
- Read `process.argv` / `process.env` outside `src/config/`
- Import Node built-ins in `src/domain/`
- Analyze the repository inside renderers or exporters
- Overwrite `.ai-docs/` files without `<!-- Generated by AI Project Docs. Safe to update. -->`
- Edit `dist/` — build artifact
- Bypass the pipeline (`executePipeline` / `ANALYSIS_PIPELINE`)
- Call `enrichProjectKnowledgeWith*` directly — use `PluginManager`
- Write non-English documentation

## Change scope

- Minimal, focused changes for the requested task
- One module at a time when possible; cross-module changes require `.ai-docs/dependency-map.md`
- Commits and PRs only when the user explicitly asks
